+# Full MCP parity inventory
+
+Legacy registry source: `src/tools.ts` (SHA-256 `b24d932e715fd7ccf94f46a9ab2cfbccfec612049394e57e5cf281509ed5e099`). The clean native checkout starts at `da8b44ee34dd349f2ae0df3f1cbae366df482354`. The source checkout did not expose a Git HEAD, so no legacy commit is claimed.
+
+The old registry defines **90 unique MCP tools and 90 unique native methods**. `name` is the externally exposed MCP name; `method` is the dotted native bridge method. Their exact descriptions, JSON Schema 7 `inputSchema`, and MCP annotations are generated from the actual Zod registry into `src/slic3r/GUI/McpToolsManifest.json`. The native implementation must preserve all runtime Zod refinements listed below because JSON Schema conversion cannot represent them.
+
+All 90 rows are compiled into the native arm64 application. The unchecked status in the table means full behavior parity for that individual tool is still pending; it does not mean no live calls were made. Independent catalog checks cover names, descriptions, schemas, and annotations. A disposable-profile run additionally verified live discovery of all 90 tools and representative safe workflows, described under [Verification boundary](#verification-boundary) and in [native acceptance](../tests/mcp/native_acceptance.md).
