+
+## Contract rules that JSON Schema does not fully express
+
+`McpToolsManifest.json` is generated with Zod-to-JSON-Schema (`jsonSchema7`, no refs). Native validation must also preserve these runtime predicates from the original TypeScript registry:
+
+- Shared `path` validator requires an absolute path and rejects NUL. It affects project paths, imports, captures, and exports that use `path`.
+- `model.import_multipart`: each path must end in `.stl` or `.obj`.
+- `object.transform`: at least one of `position`, `rotation`, or `scale` is required.
+- `plate.delete`: `targetPlateIndex` is required only when `contents="move"`, and forbidden otherwise.
+- `view.capture`, `export.geometry`, `export.gcode`, and `export.sliced_3mf`: destination suffix must respectively be `.png`, `.stl`/`.obj`, `.gcode`, and `.gcode.3mf`.
+- `settings.effective`: a plate filter requires `expectedPlateRevision`; a volume filter requires `objectId`.
+- `settings.update` and `settings.override`: values must contain 1–100 entries. `settings.override` also requires exactly the identifiers for its selected scope.
+- `object.cut`: plane normal must not be all zero.
+- `object.merge`, `painting.set`, and `slice.start_batch`: the ID, face-index, or plate-index arrays must contain unique values.
+- `ams.mapping.plan`: at least one AMS mapping is required.
+- `calibration.start`: at least one calibration routine must be selected.
+- `vector` and numeric values include finite/range checks; JSON Schema serialization may not preserve every JavaScript finite-number predicate. Native checks remain authoritative.
+
+The old native source confirms additional behavior guards: stable session-scoped model/instance/volume IDs, plate and mesh revision guards, tracked job outcomes, stale-result rejection, workspace/modal/busy mutation gating, explicit confirmation for device actions, and disabled-by-default device actions/account reads. See the corresponding old native files indicated in the table.
+
+## Verification boundary
+
+The final macOS arm64 build contains the 90-tool manifest and corresponding native handlers. The independent legacy oracle passed three catalog-contract checks, and the final executable linked. The earlier 13-tool prototype is superseded by this port.
+
+On 2026-10-05, a disposable-profile macOS run passed official MCP SDK 1.32.0 discovery of all 90 exact tool contracts, safe application/printer/model/plate/settings reads, malformed-argument checks, and default denial of all eight printer-action/cloud-read paths. A generated STL was imported with stable IDs, transformed, and saved as a valid 3MF; plate revision guards and a tracked arrange job passed. A tiny-cube slice completed, its preview contained toolpaths, G-code export wrote a file, and moving the cube made the prior slice result stale. [Native acceptance](../tests/mcp/native_acceptance.md) holds exact evidence and artifacts. This is representative workflow coverage, not execution or full behavior validation of every row.
+
+A newer arm64 build with Preferences copy-URL/show-hide changes (executable SHA-256 `2554cd3065ea28b5d3651f525e8bce539464d432cc3b984a6296d06470b7355b`) separately passed 90-tool HTTP/official-SDK discovery, default-denied sensitive paths, invalid-input checks, and safe import/transform/save/arrange in an isolated profile. A second disposable profile on this same binary passed local slice validation and tracked completion, preview toolpaths, G-code export, valid 3MF save, and stale-result rejection after a model edit. An idle process restart retained the MCP enabled state, chosen port, default-off permissions, and token identity; the renewed listener passed the safe on-phase. This did not exercise GUI Quit or GUI reopen. The subsequent Windows-export portability edit passed a 93-assertion standalone suite; its macOS preprocessed G-code implementation was confirmed byte-identical to the earlier version, and the added GUI link library is conditional on MSVC. A complete final-tree macOS arm64 Release build has since passed; its executable SHA-256 is `d1a694bdfeb07a8e7cf15b122db50a431da5e2cde7e6576cb69004b57d426bc3` (142,563,928 bytes). Windows/Linux CI remains pending.
+
+In the owned `MCP Settings Test` instance, final-bundle acceptance confirmed project reopen and visible Prepare/Preview state; Preferences enablement, default-off gates, Show/Hide, valid/invalid/occupied port behavior, enable/disable, token rotation, and GUI Quit/relaunch persistence. Official MCP SDK discovery of all 90 contracts and the safe import/transform/save/arrange/slice/preview/export/stale-result flow passed. Copy Address reported success, and pasting into the port field produced the exact `http://127.0.0.1:27948/mcp` value; the valid port was restored and the listener remained active. Windows checks remain release gates. Printer and cloud operations were denied by default and were not executed. Keep each table row unchecked until its own full behavior is verified.
